{"availability":"available","full":"andreizanik/react-mouse-select","name":"react-mouse-select","description":"A simple react library for selecting elements by moving the mouse","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":57,"forks":2,"created":"2022-07-29T13:12:20Z","updated":"2023-05-31T07:26:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://andreizanik.github.io/react-mouse-select","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.464Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.464Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.464Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.464Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome React Components","url":"https://github.com/brillout/awesome-react-components"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:27:27.501Z","stars":57,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T03:21:43.776Z","stars":57,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-15T16:59:10.341Z","stars":57,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.464Z","stars":57,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The component is designed to visualize the selection of DOM elements by moving the cursor on the screen. We leave the implementation of further interaction with selected files to you through the callback finishSelectionCallback.","This approach makes the library multipurpose because the further interaction with selected files is always unique. In one case, you need to get the Id from Datasets and update Redux-store. Otherwise, you need to add a class to the selected elements and send a request to the server. No matter how complex your case is, you can implement it with finishSelectionCallback having an array of all selected elements."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andreizanik/react-mouse-select/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"3b61e2feae682a425ef9fafd41969a4c9908d9a25c5f1a407ff9174088669937","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:27:27.501Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:18:07.46